[test-suite name=fabric
  [doc [#
conformance fixtures for cx-fabric — platform eventing, embedded tier P0
   (spec/02-working/fabric.md; #518/#531; band CXER4920-4949).

   HERMETIC. Every case rides a mem:// journal (capability-free,
   deterministic, offline). The durable plane delegates to journal (a fabric
   stream IS a journal stream): publish -> journal-append (receipt carries
   the per-stream seq), receive -> journal-since filtered by the bus §2.2
   pattern vocabulary (topic atom incl. terminal .* prefix-glob, head-name
   string, arity-1 predicate fn), ack -> cumulative committed offset
   persisted as store data through the journal's own store (the doc-backed
   alias pattern). The transient plane is latest-wins channels.

   Contract lanes: at-least-once (an uncommitted tail REDELIVERS to a fresh
   group subscription; an acked tail does not — including across fabric
   handles, proving the offset is store data, not process memory),
   observe-only refusal (CXER4922), group-less ack refusal (CXER4923),
   closed-handle refusal (CXER4921), plane/arg guards (CXER4920), and
   composition honesty (journal's own attribution/lifecycle errors surface
   verbatim, e.g. CXER4609).

   Cases 001-009 and 031-033 are the stdlib/fabric.cx [fn-doc] examples
   VERBATIM (example-backing, stdlib_docs_check). Cases 024-030 are the §9.1
   DLQ/redelivery-policy lanes (poison exhaustion, group-state inheritance,
   envelope shape, refusal lanes CXER4931); 031-036 are the §12.1
   request-reply lanes (synchronous embedded call, sticky-exclusive
   registration CXER4933, no-responder CXER4932, failure-channel
   propagation).
  #]]

 [case id=fabric-001-open-state level=core gate=enforced
  [tags fabric open handle]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/journal']
[?lib 'cx-fabric' :as fabric]
[?let [= $j [$journal:open "mem://t" "acme"]]
  [= $f [$fabric:open $j]]
  $f@state]
#]]
  [out-text [#
'open'
#]]
 ]

 [case id=fabric-002-close-then-use level=core gate=enforced
  [tags fabric close idempotent handle error]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/journal']
[?lib 'cx-fabric' :as fabric]
[?let [= $j [$journal:open "mem://t" "acme"]]
  [= $f [$fabric:open $j]]
  [= $c [$fabric:close $f]]
  [$fabric:read $f "acme/coord/map"]]
#]]
  [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER4921
#]]
 ]

